	(text "AMPLIFIER SUPPLY  (5 V LDO, fed from PACK_P so amp current bypasses R_MEAS)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 213.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "818ef269-268b-41d0-a0d6-ed8040230c2e")
	)
	(text "SLEEP-CURRENT MEASUREMENT  (both amps across R201 = R_MEAS)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "963add77-1762-432b-8911-f4f602926e3d")
	)
	(text "3.3 V ALWAYS-ON RAIL  (TPS62177, 1 MHz, sleep mode under MCU control)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a1c9286b-8f28-49a6-9d55-efbfac0d26a7")
	)
	(text "NOTES\n1. Low-current branch: PACK_P -> R201 10R -> PACK_LP -> TPS62177 -> 3V3 (MCU + both TPS25751).\n   Gauge BAT is NOT on this branch (TI: gauge must stay powered with FETs off).\n2. Kelvin-connect R202/R203 to the R201 pads.\n3. U201 gain 500: 5 mV per uA, ~0.99 mA full scale.  U202 gain 25: 0.25 V per mA, ~20 mA full scale.\n4. R202/R203/C201 fitted 0R/0R/DNP to start; 100R/100R/22nF gives a 36 kHz input filter.\n5. R204/R205 49.9R isolate the INA190 outputs from cable capacitance (1 nF max); use a 1 MOhm scope input.\n6. SLEEP low = sleep mode (internal pull-down); MCU PB4 drives it high for full load.\n7. R207 breaks the 3V3 rail for debugging.\n8. U201/U202 are hand-soldered (DigiKey/Mouser); JLC has no stock. Not in the JLC BOM/CPL.\n9. Diamonds are PWR_FLAGs (ERC only, no part): each sits where its rail is sourced through a passive part.\n10. U203 EN is left open (internal 300 nA pull-up enables it). EN must stay below 6.5 V: never tie it to LDO_IN.\n11. U204 pin 4 (NC) goes to GND, as TI recommends."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 129.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b7362222-321c-4fad-bb1b-5c18b70422bc")
	)
